WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:47.028 --> 00:00:47.649
I am...

00:00:48.028 --> 00:00:49.670
I have lost all my illusions.

00:00:49.769 --> 00:00:50.750
I expect anything.

00:00:53.492 --> 00:00:54.552
I expect anything.

00:00:58.375 --> 00:00:59.796
Nothing reassures me anymore.

00:01:03.298 --> 00:01:04.498
And especially now.

00:01:07.731 --> 00:01:08.712
Especially now.

00:01:08.812 --> 00:01:21.143
I'm so scared because everything is so uncertain that I keep thinking that from one day to the next,

00:01:22.405 --> 00:01:29.070
Something can happen before we even have time to realize it.

00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:53.283
THE

00:01:53.362 --> 00:01:57.408
Forgiveness makes no sense to me.

00:01:57.944 --> 00:02:01.165
There are some things that are absolutely unforgivable.

00:02:02.165 --> 00:02:04.266
I don't see why I should forgive them.

00:02:04.287 --> 00:02:05.287
and in particular,

00:02:05.766 --> 00:02:07.528
No one has ever asked me for forgiveness.

00:02:35.929 --> 00:02:45.473
Nothing can surprise us because we have an extremely pessimistic philosophy of humanity.

00:02:47.114 --> 00:02:54.097
I believe that men are capable of both the worst and the best.

00:02:54.317 --> 00:02:55.957
that there are two categories of men.

00:02:57.658 --> 00:02:58.899
Those who are incapable

00:03:00.881 --> 00:03:05.044
to be ferocious beasts and then those who remained primitive.

00:04:26.822 --> 00:04:26.942
And

00:04:27.062 --> 00:04:28.884
The nightmare began like this.

00:04:30.364 --> 00:04:32.444
I remember we had a bench,

00:04:33.386 --> 00:04:34.365
We were sitting,

00:04:35.487 --> 00:04:35.987
both,

00:04:36.026 --> 00:04:38.367
Because my father meant everything to me.

00:04:39.848 --> 00:04:44.850
We were leaning back to back and we were both devouring each other.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.242
And then there was a kind of furious madness,

00:04:55.144 --> 00:05:01.788
Everything was abandoned, and so people would steal from the train carriages at the station.

00:05:02.509 --> 00:05:06.612
they left with tons of cans of peas,

00:05:06.613 --> 00:05:07.394
of sardines,

00:05:07.394 --> 00:05:08.014
pasta,

00:05:08.014 --> 00:05:10.355
In short, it was really a kind of madness.

00:05:20.759 --> 00:05:22.445
We knew the danger was there.

00:05:23.028 --> 00:05:24.353
But what could we do?

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:25.717
We didn't have...

00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:28.220
Where to go?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.602
No one came to tell us,

00:05:32.022 --> 00:05:33.143
I can hide from you,

00:05:35.605 --> 00:05:39.147
Perhaps we could have done as some others have done,

00:05:39.247 --> 00:05:42.489
to try to cross the demarcation line,

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.732
But with what means?

00:05:45.832 --> 00:05:46.612
To go where?

00:05:46.892 --> 00:05:47.833
To go somewhere else?

00:05:48.274 --> 00:05:48.453
Good,

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:49.674
We stayed.

00:06:07.939 --> 00:06:09.560
And everything was forbidden.

00:06:09.562 --> 00:06:11.242
We shouldn't have left the city.

00:06:11.421 --> 00:06:13.502
We shouldn't have gathered together.

00:06:13.582 --> 00:06:18.485
You shouldn't go out in the street at just any time of day.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:23.288
And outside, one could hear cries from the bone,

00:06:23.389 --> 00:06:23.688
the bone,

00:06:23.748 --> 00:06:24.188
schnell,

00:06:24.288 --> 00:06:24.748
schnell,

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:29.911
heraus and machine gun fire.

00:06:33.053 --> 00:06:33.875
But all of that,

00:06:33.995 --> 00:06:35.055
It's happening.

00:06:36.579 --> 00:06:40.061
It seems so unreal,

00:06:40.181 --> 00:06:42.022
We don't know if we're dreaming.

00:06:42.102 --> 00:06:43.483
if that's the reality.

00:06:48.626 --> 00:06:50.247
I was completely paralyzed,

00:06:50.248 --> 00:06:51.608
There were only corpses.

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:54.350
There was just one baby,

00:06:56.151 --> 00:06:57.491
I knew that baby well,

00:06:57.632 --> 00:06:58.692
He was 18 months old.

00:07:00.613 --> 00:07:02.935
who was screaming amidst his corpses.

00:07:07.047 --> 00:07:08.087
There was a lot of blood.

00:07:10.008 --> 00:07:13.389
I couldn't move my body.

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:17.351
And this baby,

00:07:17.491 --> 00:07:28.535
It haunts me to this day because I feel a little guilty for not having had the strength to go and get that child.

00:07:29.991 --> 00:07:37.396
Resistance had grown throughout this period, and German officers were beginning to be killed here and there.

00:07:37.737 --> 00:07:38.337
in Paris,

00:07:38.377 --> 00:07:38.877
in Nantes,

00:07:38.878 --> 00:07:39.318
in Bordeaux.

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:42.300
I mainly did transport of equipment.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.001
of all kinds,

00:07:45.082 --> 00:07:47.584
newspapers and sometimes weapons,

00:07:48.304 --> 00:07:50.206
Sticks of dynamite or things like that,

00:07:50.306 --> 00:07:53.868
panniers from my bike to take them here and there.

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:56.490
I was mainly part of the armed group.

00:07:59.363 --> 00:08:04.127
The application of Pétain's anti-Semitic legislation,

00:08:04.807 --> 00:08:08.330
which he put in place as early as October 1940,

00:08:08.971 --> 00:08:11.673
will be implemented gradually.

00:08:12.914 --> 00:08:13.694
It didn't...

00:08:14.764 --> 00:08:21.187
I played so much on my father's arrest on December 12, 1941,

00:08:21.288 --> 00:08:24.971
because he was arrested by the Germans,

00:08:25.011 --> 00:08:25.891
by the Gestapo

00:08:26.091 --> 00:08:30.153
as a hostage among a thousand prominent Jews.

00:08:30.935 --> 00:08:32.975
And me and my mother,

00:08:33.036 --> 00:08:37.918
We will be taken on July 16th.

00:08:39.339 --> 00:08:46.804
1942 as part of the arafle which you know as the Veldif arafle.

00:08:54.049 --> 00:09:00.934
We were evicted from our home along with the others.

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:05.739
all the Jews were herded into a neighborhood.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.901
There was ghetto A and ghetto B.

00:09:10.322 --> 00:09:22.312
Ghetto A consisted of young people who were fit for work and useful to the

00:09:22.711 --> 00:09:23.293
3rd rail,

00:09:23.773 --> 00:09:24.754
to production.

00:09:26.676 --> 00:09:31.379
And ghetto B was packed with people who didn't have time.

00:09:32.259 --> 00:09:33.160
deport them,

00:09:34.121 --> 00:09:35.502
nor assassinate them.

00:09:38.284 --> 00:09:40.606
So, families who were bringing things back from elsewhere.

00:09:41.168 --> 00:09:41.908
And those people,

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:45.070
They didn't care about them at all.

00:09:46.531 --> 00:09:47.913
There were no supplies,

00:09:47.952 --> 00:09:48.713
There was nothing there.

00:09:49.654 --> 00:09:51.656
When the doorbell rang at our door

00:09:52.456 --> 00:09:54.118
July 16th, morning,

00:09:55.219 --> 00:09:56.500
I could have chosen not to open it.

00:09:57.521 --> 00:09:59.382
But my mother told me "open it".

00:10:00.403 --> 00:10:02.365
We had prepared some things,

00:10:02.366 --> 00:10:04.127
We didn't know what was going to happen.

00:10:04.668 --> 00:10:06.009
And in front of our door,

00:10:06.068 --> 00:10:09.873
There were French police officers.

00:10:15.518 --> 00:10:22.923
And I would also like to remind everyone that on that day, only foreign or stateless Jews were rounded up.

00:10:24.985 --> 00:10:26.388
it was kind of the...

00:10:27.469 --> 00:10:34.374
The screen or the protection of the French Israelites.

00:10:35.855 --> 00:10:38.997
And what I saw was something atrocious.

00:10:39.097 --> 00:10:41.319
There were corpses in the streets,

00:10:41.439 --> 00:10:43.720
They were just kids holding hands,

00:10:45.021 --> 00:10:49.184
with the snotty-nosed child in tears,

00:10:50.345 --> 00:10:51.786
who wandered the streets,

00:10:52.046 --> 00:10:54.048
They probably had no one left.

00:10:54.268 --> 00:10:55.429
that they no longer had parents.

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:00.466
In this closed ghetto,

00:11:00.467 --> 00:11:02.487
It was just me and my two brothers,

00:11:03.647 --> 00:11:05.428
No one from the family left.

00:11:06.609 --> 00:11:07.850
Everyone was deported.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:08.810
assassinated.

00:11:21.958 --> 00:11:23.299
When the door opened,

00:11:23.499 --> 00:11:23.979
I saw

00:11:24.659 --> 00:11:25.460
Goldilocks,

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.560
I knew it was over.

00:11:28.898 --> 00:11:32.360
So he recognized me immediately, of course.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:36.363
but he didn't report me within a minute.

00:11:36.803 --> 00:11:37.563
It has settled down,

00:11:37.724 --> 00:11:39.265
It looked like a wounded animal.

00:11:39.345 --> 00:11:42.627
Then he looked at each girl individually and said no.

00:11:42.707 --> 00:11:42.827
No.

00:11:43.448 --> 00:11:45.590
I was saying, as long as they don't recognize me.

00:11:46.251 --> 00:11:48.153
I prayed to God that they wouldn't recognize me.

00:11:49.094 --> 00:11:51.618
And then finally he made up his mind and then he chose me.

00:11:51.638 --> 00:11:52.439
He said it was her.

00:11:53.059 --> 00:11:54.060
Then the German said,

00:11:54.621 --> 00:11:55.262
the German, sorry.

00:11:57.084 --> 00:11:57.825
the guy with the mouth.

00:11:57.825 --> 00:11:58.526
The Gestapo said

00:11:59.847 --> 00:12:00.367
"It's Annick."

00:12:01.748 --> 00:12:02.909
The head of the office said "no,

00:12:02.949 --> 00:12:03.069
No,

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.090
her name is not

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.313
"Annick." She declined to give my name.

00:12:07.553 --> 00:12:10.515
And then they took me to the

00:12:11.076 --> 00:12:13.358
The Gestapo, which was three steps further on,

00:12:13.618 --> 00:12:14.799
on the same street opposite.

00:12:15.479 --> 00:12:18.762
Two others recognized me again.

00:12:19.422 --> 00:12:20.783
There were 24 of us arrested.

00:12:22.785 --> 00:12:25.567
Those two who recognized me didn't talk much.

00:12:25.948 --> 00:12:27.469
They did not overwhelm us.

00:12:27.529 --> 00:12:27.649
THANKS.

00:12:27.649 --> 00:12:34.153
But really, the Germans were fully aware of our entire organization.

00:12:34.173 --> 00:12:35.314
of our activities,

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:37.035
They were fully aware of everything.

00:12:37.156 --> 00:12:43.940
We were ordered to assemble in a large square,

00:12:44.901 --> 00:12:47.803
This was the old bus station.

00:12:50.285 --> 00:12:55.248
and we were forced to kneel with our hands behind our necks.

00:12:57.113 --> 00:12:59.094
And they proceeded with the selection.

00:13:03.076 --> 00:13:06.458
That's how, in the liquidation of the ghetto,

00:13:06.618 --> 00:13:07.279
My brother

00:13:07.919 --> 00:13:09.540
Kadek has disappeared.

00:13:17.124 --> 00:13:17.964
And next to me,

00:13:17.984 --> 00:13:21.906
There was a woman I knew.

00:13:23.968 --> 00:13:25.288
She had just had a baby.

00:13:26.689 --> 00:13:28.170
This baby was 15 days old.

00:13:29.811 --> 00:13:30.972
She was next to me,

00:13:31.132 --> 00:13:34.354
They ordered him to stand up.

00:13:34.734 --> 00:13:35.434
to move forward.

00:13:37.015 --> 00:13:39.057
And given that she had the baby,

00:13:39.357 --> 00:13:39.977
necessarily,

00:13:40.057 --> 00:13:43.639
She was going to the group that we knew wasn't good.

00:13:46.181 --> 00:13:48.422
And nothing was happening calmly.

00:13:48.963 --> 00:13:49.903
Each person...

00:13:52.969 --> 00:13:55.391
He indicated his direction.

00:13:56.112 --> 00:13:57.172
a lash of the whip,

00:13:57.192 --> 00:13:58.153
a kick,

00:13:59.594 --> 00:14:00.455
And that woman,

00:14:00.575 --> 00:14:01.476
She tripped.

00:14:04.358 --> 00:14:05.419
And the baby fell.

00:14:11.204 --> 00:14:12.305
And two soldiers,

00:14:13.726 --> 00:14:14.947
They were probably drunk.

00:14:14.987 --> 00:14:16.868
It's impossible that it was any other way.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:21.192
They started playing football with this child.

00:14:22.845 --> 00:14:23.526
And this mother,

00:14:23.566 --> 00:14:28.930
She turned around and received a blow to the head with a whip.

00:14:29.951 --> 00:14:30.732
And she left.

00:14:47.861 --> 00:14:49.323
On September 25th,

00:14:50.004 --> 00:14:53.949
when we were made to get off our wagons at Bestiaux,

00:14:56.533 --> 00:14:59.276
They separated us men.

00:15:00.529 --> 00:15:01.210
and women.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:02.191
Afterwards,

00:15:02.231 --> 00:15:07.436
In the middle of the ramp, there were covered trucks that had stopped.

00:15:07.897 --> 00:15:10.719
towards which the children were directed,

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.541
the old people,

00:15:13.242 --> 00:15:14.323
disabled people,

00:15:14.423 --> 00:15:15.484
the injured,

00:15:15.564 --> 00:15:16.725
elderly people.

00:15:17.526 --> 00:15:23.092
I didn't even see my mother get into the truck.

00:15:24.386 --> 00:15:26.489
And we left.

00:15:27.791 --> 00:15:28.572
afterwards,

00:15:29.073 --> 00:15:33.299
We counted ourselves in a convoy of 1000 men.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:34.361
women,

00:15:35.222 --> 00:15:35.682
children,

00:15:36.303 --> 00:15:39.708
only 26 women at the Birkenau camp.

00:15:44.242 --> 00:15:45.342
We didn't understand anything.

00:15:45.403 --> 00:15:50.545
We were starting to wonder why the trucks hadn't arrived before us.

00:15:50.565 --> 00:15:57.527
And when we asked the hood why the trucks weren't arriving,

00:15:57.648 --> 00:16:01.489
She gestured for us to go towards the windows.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.570
And looking out the windows,

00:16:04.571 --> 00:16:07.892
She showed us chimneys that were smoking.

00:16:08.812 --> 00:16:12.073
And she immediately explained to us that...

00:16:13.854 --> 00:16:18.435
Those who had not followed us on foot into the camp,

00:16:20.196 --> 00:16:21.416
They had passed by there.

00:16:21.476 --> 00:16:31.379
She told us about the gas chambers and crematoria that were smoking and turning the sky red.

00:16:31.679 --> 00:16:31.919
SO,

00:16:32.759 --> 00:16:35.120
practically the evening of my arrival,

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:38.141
I knew I would never see my mother again.

00:16:38.142 --> 00:16:43.202
I still held onto hope of finding my father.

00:16:44.502 --> 00:16:55.645
So we spent our first night in this sauna block because the initiation ceremonies didn't start until the next day.

00:16:56.086 --> 00:16:59.106
I forgot to mention that on the day of our arrival,

00:16:59.206 --> 00:16:59.327
THE

00:17:00.147 --> 00:17:01.367
September 25

00:17:03.628 --> 00:17:04.428
1942 my mother,

00:17:04.429 --> 00:17:05.868
It was his birthday.

00:17:05.908 --> 00:17:07.289
She was just 50 years old.

00:17:19.354 --> 00:17:21.295
We were stripped naked,

00:17:21.615 --> 00:17:26.437
They shaved our heads and they tattooed us.

00:17:28.178 --> 00:17:31.959
And that's what Auschwitz was special about.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:33.740
The tattoo,

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:34.480
that's to say...

00:17:36.781 --> 00:17:36.921
Good,

00:17:36.981 --> 00:17:39.102
My mother told me that as soon as we arrived.

00:17:39.162 --> 00:17:42.424
when we put down our handbag,

00:17:43.524 --> 00:17:44.965
that we no longer had an identity,

00:17:45.205 --> 00:17:45.765
That was true.

00:17:59.698 --> 00:18:00.098
One fine day,

00:18:00.099 --> 00:18:00.999
We met up again,

00:18:01.079 --> 00:18:01.940
the 24th,

00:18:04.562 --> 00:18:05.362
in trucks,

00:18:06.623 --> 00:18:07.504
on buses,

00:18:07.584 --> 00:18:08.285
I believe, moreover,

00:18:08.665 --> 00:18:12.268
and then on a train that took us to Frennes.

00:18:12.568 --> 00:18:14.129
All 24 of us were together.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:24.853
We were shown into an extremely well-laid-out room,

00:18:24.893 --> 00:18:27.155
Black and red flags everywhere

00:18:27.156 --> 00:18:28.916
Hitler's portrait at the very back,

00:18:29.756 --> 00:18:32.238
the judges in their full judicial robes.

00:18:32.818 --> 00:18:34.460
It was extremely impressive.

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:36.801
There were soldiers all along the walls.

00:18:37.402 --> 00:18:38.182
They make us stand up,

00:18:38.282 --> 00:18:39.103
They make us get up.

00:18:39.584 --> 00:18:41.545
And then begins the spiel.

00:18:41.665 --> 00:18:43.667
the president of the court.

00:18:43.707 --> 00:18:44.808
And gradually,

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:51.573
The interpreter repeated what the president was saying.

00:18:52.734 --> 00:18:53.655
The first nine,

00:18:54.235 --> 00:18:55.175
And I wasn't one of them.

00:18:55.776 --> 00:18:56.616
sentenced to death.

00:18:56.876 --> 00:18:58.897
It certainly made quite an impression on me.

00:18:59.818 --> 00:19:01.899
But all of a sudden I thought I wasn't going to be.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:04.761
Besides, I never thought I would be sentenced to death.

00:19:04.762 --> 00:19:07.322
I didn't think I was strong enough for that.

00:19:08.223 --> 00:19:13.085
The first nine people sentenced to death for aggression against the German army,

00:19:13.626 --> 00:19:14.906
equipment deterioration

00:19:14.986 --> 00:19:15.127
etc.

00:19:15.947 --> 00:19:16.107
Good,

00:19:16.527 --> 00:19:19.769
and they continue for the next seven.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:21.471
They were also sentenced to death.

00:19:21.571 --> 00:19:22.011
So, them,

00:19:22.091 --> 00:19:25.053
for assistance to the enemies of Germany,

00:19:25.073 --> 00:19:26.114
to those who were degrading,

00:19:26.194 --> 00:19:27.375
We had assisted them.

00:19:27.715 --> 00:19:28.996
I was one of those seven.

00:19:29.016 --> 00:19:33.819
The beach of

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.181
Goethe, the camp commandant,

00:19:39.303 --> 00:19:41.484
He enjoyed shooting people.

00:19:42.205 --> 00:19:43.406
He arrived at a gallop,

00:19:44.847 --> 00:19:45.847
on a white horse,

00:19:47.849 --> 00:19:48.709
with a dog.

00:19:49.874 --> 00:19:57.716
of Almatian who followed the horse and then he shot at everything that moved.

00:20:01.377 --> 00:20:02.098
And that's how it is.

00:20:03.158 --> 00:20:03.578
A day,

00:20:03.638 --> 00:20:11.440
There was a woman who fell at my feet and I turned around,

00:20:14.781 --> 00:20:15.822
I was watching him.

00:20:17.462 --> 00:20:19.524
And I saw that he was thriving.

00:20:21.405 --> 00:20:22.606
He was pleased with himself.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.771
And he had...

00:20:30.252 --> 00:20:31.773
He had fantasies like that.

00:20:34.755 --> 00:20:36.277
He was quite a character...

00:20:38.759 --> 00:20:40.300
Throughout my deportation,

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:41.561
from all sides...

00:20:43.282 --> 00:20:43.922
the most,

00:20:44.162 --> 00:20:48.744
I don't dare say the craziest one because it wouldn't be his fault if I said he was crazy.

00:20:52.006 --> 00:20:53.506
but the most bestial,

00:20:53.887 --> 00:20:55.747
I don't know what it was made of.

00:20:55.907 --> 00:20:58.168
But he loved blood,

00:20:59.669 --> 00:21:00.990
Barbarity killed.

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:03.831
It was,

00:21:06.132 --> 00:21:10.494
I read afterwards that he was a very ordinary man.

00:21:11.694 --> 00:21:14.076
And it's often ordinary men,

00:21:16.197 --> 00:21:19.080
who gained a certain amount of power during the war,

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.402
who allowed themselves the most horrible things.

00:21:38.358 --> 00:21:44.040
I always believed that it wasn't only the Germans who could be capable of things like that.

00:21:44.881 --> 00:21:46.181
In France, too, one could be like that.

00:21:46.201 --> 00:21:46.982
And you can see the proof.

00:21:47.322 --> 00:21:48.902
They tortured people in Algeria.

00:21:49.043 --> 00:21:49.303
we have...

00:21:55.365 --> 00:22:00.667
My despair over painful events is not limited to what is happening in Europe.

00:22:01.768 --> 00:22:02.168
everywhere,

00:22:02.448 --> 00:22:05.229
both in South America and in Africa.

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:13.875
anywhere in the world where there are crimes like the one in Rwanda.

00:22:15.176 --> 00:22:20.160
Of course it provoked our anger.

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:20.941
our sadness,

00:22:21.001 --> 00:22:22.242
Our despair too.

00:22:22.942 --> 00:22:25.604
Having lived,

00:22:26.725 --> 00:22:32.069
It still seems crazy to me that things like that could happen after the Second World War.

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:34.331
But like everyone else,

00:22:34.871 --> 00:22:35.512
no doubt

00:22:36.772 --> 00:22:38.253
We get used to the worst.

00:22:38.254 --> 00:22:39.734
I don't know how to explain it.

00:22:41.815 --> 00:22:42.435
It's painful.

00:22:42.515 --> 00:22:42.636
Yes,

00:22:42.696 --> 00:22:43.136
That's for sure.

00:22:43.356 --> 00:22:47.378
A profound pain, even.

00:22:48.819 --> 00:22:48.939
Me,

00:22:49.039 --> 00:22:49.860
personally,

00:22:50.980 --> 00:22:59.225
I have never denied that there were genocides before the Nazi camps and that there have been genocides since.

00:23:01.466 --> 00:23:09.814
I know that not all of my colleagues will agree to even using the expression "concentration camp".

00:23:10.335 --> 00:23:15.580
which they readily reserve for extermination in the Nazi camp,

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:19.163
But it exists elsewhere and in other forms.

00:23:19.664 --> 00:23:20.164
Of course.

00:23:20.985 --> 00:23:24.448
I do not hold young Germans responsible,

00:23:25.909 --> 00:23:30.853
even though I know that there are still far-right groups.

00:23:31.794 --> 00:23:33.716
There are Nazis in Germany.

00:23:34.376 --> 00:23:34.696
But anyway,

00:23:34.816 --> 00:23:36.017
There are some in France too.

00:23:47.046 --> 00:23:49.648
The Battle of Stalingrad would reverse the course of history.

00:23:51.665 --> 00:23:52.305
In a few months,

00:23:52.545 --> 00:23:55.127
The flag of the Soviet Union will once again fly over the city.

00:24:04.792 --> 00:24:09.695
50,000 Russian soldiers and almost three times as many German soldiers would lose their lives on the battlefield.

00:24:11.216 --> 00:24:12.776
Another 120,000 will be taken prisoner.

00:24:17.439 --> 00:24:20.501
The defeat of the German 6th Army will shake the Third Reich.

00:24:26.175 --> 00:24:26.535
SO,

00:24:27.096 --> 00:24:32.358
We would put our ear to the ground to feel if the earth was resonating.

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:45.364
And that's where they gradually began sending people to Auschwitz.

00:24:54.429 --> 00:24:55.430
We were all naked.

00:24:58.474 --> 00:24:59.295
We were afraid.

00:24:59.636 --> 00:25:00.356
because there,

00:25:01.638 --> 00:25:04.562
We were overwhelmed by the smell and the smoke.

00:25:06.344 --> 00:25:07.345
And it was nervous,

00:25:07.425 --> 00:25:08.627
We were banging on it.

00:25:11.077 --> 00:25:13.859
They were doing it to us.

00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:17.421
since there was no way to go to the toilet.

00:25:17.422 --> 00:25:18.882
And then perhaps fear,

00:25:21.224 --> 00:25:22.425
It was hellish.

00:25:23.445 --> 00:25:25.046
All the smells mingled.

00:25:26.748 --> 00:25:27.409
One fine morning,

00:25:27.509 --> 00:25:27.949
very early on,

00:25:28.390 --> 00:25:28.911
at dawn,

00:25:29.151 --> 00:25:30.292
We heard a noise.

00:25:32.194 --> 00:25:32.995
We were very scared.

00:25:33.736 --> 00:25:35.018
It stopped at our cell.

00:25:35.338 --> 00:25:35.739
We said to ourselves,

00:25:35.759 --> 00:25:36.139
That's it.

00:25:36.600 --> 00:25:40.865
And the guy came and read us something that said the 14 boys were...

00:25:40.945 --> 00:25:43.708
They were shot within the hour, and we were...

00:25:44.589 --> 00:25:45.911
that we would be sent to Germany,

00:25:46.151 --> 00:25:54.000
that the Führer in his great kindness was granting us a respite, we were not pardoned, and that our fate would depend on our attitude in Germany.

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:58.405
So I stayed in Lübeck for three months and then after three months we were

00:25:59.606 --> 00:26:02.828
An entire group from Lubeck prison was sent to Côte-Bus.

00:26:03.308 --> 00:26:04.509
And on July 14th,

00:26:04.609 --> 00:26:05.850
we told our caretakers,

00:26:06.450 --> 00:26:08.392
Today is the national holiday and we are on strike.

00:26:08.393 --> 00:26:09.112
We are not working.

00:26:09.813 --> 00:26:10.893
And that's what we did.

00:26:11.013 --> 00:26:12.094
Then we danced,

00:26:12.254 --> 00:26:12.594
sung,

00:26:13.335 --> 00:26:14.956
The Marseillaise was born in Nipotin.

00:26:16.537 --> 00:26:17.198
And there you have it.

00:26:17.658 --> 00:26:18.879
The Gestapo came.

00:26:19.399 --> 00:26:20.620
They regretted it a great deal,

00:26:20.660 --> 00:26:21.220
the guards,

00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:23.142
because afterwards the Gestapo was there every day.

00:26:23.782 --> 00:26:25.763
And that's where our fate took a turn.

00:26:25.903 --> 00:26:28.205
that shortly afterwards we were sent to Ravendzourek.

00:26:32.346 --> 00:26:38.848
We were lined up between the electrified barbed wire and the barracks.

00:26:41.029 --> 00:26:46.891
We were told to undress and between two rows of

00:26:47.231 --> 00:26:50.752
SS, we were made to run for our lives.

00:26:52.852 --> 00:26:53.232
SO...

00:26:55.145 --> 00:27:00.348
This race can be summarized as follows:

00:27:00.408 --> 00:27:11.614
because we knew approximately that at the start there were 6000 of us and at the finish there were 1500 of us.

00:27:13.936 --> 00:27:15.456
And the missing ones...

00:27:16.381 --> 00:27:26.106
We had been pushed out of the line of this race with rifle butts by the SS on both sides.

00:27:29.328 --> 00:27:30.348
We met up again,

00:27:30.888 --> 00:27:33.350
I don't know exactly which space,

00:27:34.130 --> 00:27:43.275
and we were harangued by the camp commander who told us that we had been chosen to live.

00:27:44.195 --> 00:27:56.438
while we saw the trucks on which thousands of our comrades were being loaded, who were going to die that day,

00:27:57.538 --> 00:28:00.739
and that they were taken to the gas chambers,

00:28:00.819 --> 00:28:02.919
that we could hear screaming,

00:28:02.959 --> 00:28:08.581
so that I don't remember anything else from the speech.

00:28:09.985 --> 00:28:18.671
from the camp commandant because we could hear our comrades screaming their heads off because there,

00:28:19.611 --> 00:28:22.353
They knew where they were going.

00:28:26.035 --> 00:28:28.296
We can't say what we...

00:28:29.785 --> 00:28:36.749
What exactly one feels when standing in this complex in front of the crematorium,

00:28:36.809 --> 00:28:37.909
with that smell,

00:28:39.090 --> 00:28:39.931
this smoke,

00:28:43.412 --> 00:28:46.394
and that you are waiting for

00:28:51.297 --> 00:28:52.898
How long will this last?

00:28:52.938 --> 00:28:53.618
We don't know.

00:28:56.099 --> 00:28:57.380
Am I going to collapse?

00:28:57.460 --> 00:28:58.200
I don't know.

00:29:02.446 --> 00:29:06.028
It's impossible to describe what you feel in that moment.

00:29:11.773 --> 00:29:13.314
It's something unreal.

00:29:20.419 --> 00:29:22.080
It was a smell of...

00:29:23.861 --> 00:29:24.521
Of death,

00:29:24.561 --> 00:29:25.342
Please,

00:29:25.382 --> 00:29:26.642
of misery,

00:29:26.702 --> 00:29:26.822
of...

00:29:27.343 --> 00:29:27.783
I don't know,

00:29:27.843 --> 00:29:28.583
It was a smell...

00:29:29.383 --> 00:29:29.503
Me,

00:29:29.583 --> 00:29:33.305
I was enveloped by the smell for a long time.

00:29:33.345 --> 00:29:33.705
a long time.

00:29:34.646 --> 00:29:35.166
I remember,

00:29:35.167 --> 00:29:39.508
a woman who was murmuring a prayer.

00:29:40.688 --> 00:29:42.209
I was angry after that.

00:29:44.570 --> 00:29:45.030
And then,

00:29:45.050 --> 00:29:46.831
there had been a spring,

00:29:46.832 --> 00:29:47.291
You see,

00:29:47.571 --> 00:29:50.232
I suddenly regained my strength.

00:29:50.432 --> 00:29:51.213
my anger.

00:29:52.677 --> 00:29:53.137
I was thinking,

00:29:53.157 --> 00:29:54.678
But how can she pray?

00:29:55.359 --> 00:29:58.740
But how can she think that there is a God?

00:30:02.022 --> 00:30:03.043
I was outraged.

00:30:04.263 --> 00:30:09.186
And I am a rebel against religion.

00:30:09.746 --> 00:30:10.567
even now,

00:30:11.347 --> 00:30:13.308
whereas I would like to respect.

00:30:15.333 --> 00:30:16.514
Some religions,

00:30:16.534 --> 00:30:18.016
There are some very good people,

00:30:18.757 --> 00:30:20.499
We need to believe in something.

00:30:20.599 --> 00:30:21.119
hang.

00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:23.622
I put myself in the place of those people,

00:30:24.042 --> 00:30:25.344
It helps them to live.

00:30:28.427 --> 00:30:30.989
But when I think that our executioners were believers,

00:30:31.250 --> 00:30:33.272
that they greeted each other,

00:30:33.893 --> 00:30:34.914
"God with us",

00:30:35.975 --> 00:30:36.936
God with us.

00:30:39.501 --> 00:30:43.702
Without being able to project themselves into the future,

00:30:43.862 --> 00:30:47.264
without believing there would be a future,

00:30:48.384 --> 00:30:49.624
We couldn't survive.

00:30:50.185 --> 00:31:02.909
But I knew there were political organizations in the camp, so I asked to join the clandestine organization.

00:31:03.929 --> 00:31:07.071
let's say from a French-speaking communist party,

00:31:07.371 --> 00:31:10.212
because there were French women,

00:31:10.213 --> 00:31:11.533
There were Belgians,

00:31:11.573 --> 00:31:18.636
At that time there were Dutch women who made up the group.

00:31:20.777 --> 00:31:21.877
of French language.

00:31:22.858 --> 00:31:24.258
We arrived in a block,

00:31:24.278 --> 00:31:25.038
block 32,

00:31:25.298 --> 00:31:26.959
which had already been working for a long time.

00:31:27.259 --> 00:31:29.619
So there was already a sense of solidarity in place.

00:31:30.020 --> 00:31:31.060
So, solidarity,

00:31:31.160 --> 00:31:36.081
It was indeed the communists who had initially organized it.

00:31:36.082 --> 00:31:37.382
A lot of pregnant women arrived.

00:31:37.402 --> 00:31:38.362
So, initially,

00:31:38.702 --> 00:31:39.282
They were killed.

00:31:39.462 --> 00:31:41.823
she and the baby.

00:31:42.703 --> 00:31:43.303
And then,

00:31:43.443 --> 00:31:44.864
We only killed babies.

00:31:45.704 --> 00:31:46.464
I don't know why,

00:31:46.465 --> 00:31:48.665
instead of killing them upon arrival,

00:31:48.765 --> 00:31:50.185
We were waiting until they had had the baby.

00:31:50.465 --> 00:31:51.205
They killed them both.

00:31:51.565 --> 00:31:52.006
Then afterwards,

00:31:52.007 --> 00:31:53.126
We only killed the baby.

00:31:53.226 --> 00:31:53.586
Then afterwards,

00:31:53.587 --> 00:31:55.047
We let them live.

00:31:55.167 --> 00:31:57.187
The children were dying like flies.

00:31:57.348 --> 00:31:58.528
We gave milk to the dogs,

00:31:58.548 --> 00:31:59.348
but not to children.

00:32:03.090 --> 00:32:03.310
SO,

00:32:03.690 --> 00:32:08.192
A pair of rubber gloves was stolen from the German doctors.

00:32:08.572 --> 00:32:10.692
And we made pacifiers out of the gloves.

00:32:11.653 --> 00:32:11.993
It was...

00:32:12.617 --> 00:32:14.258
Very complex and very diverse,

00:32:14.758 --> 00:32:15.619
solidarity.

00:32:16.139 --> 00:32:19.380
Nevertheless, not many children were saved.

00:32:19.460 --> 00:32:21.521
even risking his life to help them.

00:32:22.582 --> 00:32:23.682
Go steal the dog's milk,

00:32:23.762 --> 00:32:24.923
It was incredibly dangerous.

00:32:28.484 --> 00:32:37.068
Living conditions were such that survival time was all the more limited because...

00:32:39.341 --> 00:32:41.582
The food was insufficient.

00:32:42.923 --> 00:32:44.404
The lice were there.

00:32:45.705 --> 00:32:47.106
The work was there.

00:32:47.486 --> 00:32:48.707
The dogs were there.

00:32:49.527 --> 00:32:59.333
The guards and overseers who monitored the internal life of the camp and who accompanied the commandos on their way to work,

00:32:59.813 --> 00:33:03.796
Everything was done to make us die.

00:33:04.236 --> 00:33:04.976
We were able to...

00:33:06.696 --> 00:33:09.218
Resist until you catch typhus.

00:33:10.899 --> 00:33:11.059
Good,

00:33:11.179 --> 00:33:16.742
I had already seen lice under a microscope in parasitology.

00:33:18.063 --> 00:33:24.527
But then we discovered that we have no time.

00:33:24.547 --> 00:33:28.609
We were covered in lice.

00:33:28.810 --> 00:33:31.691
And it's the louse that transmits the...

00:33:34.056 --> 00:33:35.777
Exanthematic typhus.

00:33:38.257 --> 00:33:39.558
The trucks have arrived.

00:33:40.018 --> 00:33:42.438
And then tragedy struck.

00:33:43.499 --> 00:33:45.399
We put the children in the truck,

00:33:45.899 --> 00:33:48.200
They were torn away from their mothers who were holding them like that,

00:33:48.800 --> 00:33:51.001
And we watched helplessly as it happened.

00:33:52.221 --> 00:33:52.941
It was horrific.

00:33:53.041 --> 00:33:56.962
Afterwards we were so ashamed of having let it happen.

00:33:58.523 --> 00:33:58.903
But anyway,

00:33:59.143 --> 00:34:00.523
It was absolutely...

00:34:00.803 --> 00:34:02.224
That's my worst memory.

00:34:03.372 --> 00:34:03.492
Yes,

00:34:05.213 --> 00:34:05.574
this time,

00:34:05.874 --> 00:34:06.154
they have...

00:34:06.494 --> 00:34:09.216
Then the children were put into the trucks.

00:34:09.296 --> 00:34:11.538
The trucks left and, strangely enough,

00:34:12.238 --> 00:34:14.680
The mothers were screaming, but the children weren't.

00:34:15.120 --> 00:34:18.142
The little twig who was playing with the mess...

00:34:18.282 --> 00:34:22.803
The camp leader was clinging to his mother's neck; he didn't shed a tear.

00:34:22.903 --> 00:34:36.686
Nothing at all, the camp leader who had just been playing with him snatched her from her mother by the hair, gave the woman a hard blow with a goumi stick, and she collapsed to the ground, unconscious.

00:34:37.326 --> 00:34:46.268
I kept thinking, 'Please let her be dead, it's going to be terrible, waking up without her little one, it was awful, really.'

00:34:47.695 --> 00:34:49.077
That was the hardest part for me.

00:34:49.077 --> 00:34:49.177
That.

00:34:49.217 --> 00:34:52.018
I feel no guilt.

00:34:52.637 --> 00:34:52.958
But here,

00:34:54.039 --> 00:34:54.878
I'm a little ashamed.

00:34:55.259 --> 00:34:56.260
I think we should have,

00:34:56.820 --> 00:34:58.581
even at the risk of being massacred,

00:34:59.101 --> 00:34:59.861
to revolt,

00:35:00.320 --> 00:35:01.061
to do something.

00:35:01.722 --> 00:35:02.481
We did nothing.

00:35:03.983 --> 00:35:04.103
Yes,

00:35:04.202 --> 00:35:04.722
We should have.

00:35:12.312 --> 00:35:13.573
In fact, we were in tears.

00:35:13.673 --> 00:35:14.213
it must be said,

00:35:14.893 --> 00:35:15.774
We were in tears.

00:35:22.957 --> 00:35:24.638
The Allied armies land in Normandy.

00:35:32.382 --> 00:35:33.762
The blood and tears of thousands of men,

00:35:33.982 --> 00:35:34.863
civilians and military personnel,

00:35:34.883 --> 00:35:36.904
intertwine in one of the greatest battles in history.

00:35:45.524 --> 00:35:46.024
In a few months,

00:35:46.025 --> 00:35:47.185
France will be liberated.

00:35:51.908 --> 00:35:52.448
For some,

00:35:52.868 --> 00:35:53.609
This is the end of the war.

00:35:54.709 --> 00:35:55.210
For others,

00:35:55.330 --> 00:35:56.290
at the gates of hell,

00:35:56.550 --> 00:35:58.472
Peace and freedom are still only a hope.

00:36:00.013 --> 00:36:04.795
And we were evacuated from Auschwitz,

00:36:05.396 --> 00:36:06.156
all camps,

00:36:06.757 --> 00:36:07.977
of the entire complex.

00:36:09.298 --> 00:36:09.858
Initially,

00:36:09.878 --> 00:36:10.979
That made us happy.

00:36:12.816 --> 00:36:14.758
We knew we weren't going to be gassed,

00:36:16.099 --> 00:36:17.800
because that had been our fear.

00:36:18.641 --> 00:36:19.081
Only,

00:36:20.082 --> 00:36:21.563
We were being shot at.

00:36:22.124 --> 00:36:23.625
When we could no longer move forward,

00:36:23.645 --> 00:36:25.206
We saw our comrades falling.

00:36:25.226 --> 00:36:29.049
That's why we called all these marches towards other camps,

00:36:29.570 --> 00:36:31.431
the death marches.

00:36:32.612 --> 00:36:35.255
That's how I got started.

00:36:38.104 --> 00:36:38.865
At the end of January,

00:36:38.925 --> 00:36:39.885
early February,

00:36:39.906 --> 00:36:41.146
at the Ravensbrück camp,

00:36:41.566 --> 00:36:42.487
under a tent.

00:36:43.327 --> 00:36:46.269
We were wading through water up to our mid-thighs,

00:36:46.429 --> 00:36:48.230
That's why we were so cold.

00:36:48.670 --> 00:36:49.871
We no longer had a straw mattress,

00:36:49.911 --> 00:36:51.452
only a few planks.

00:36:52.753 --> 00:36:55.914
Four of us slept on the planks.

00:36:55.954 --> 00:37:01.858
So survival and hope were not yet forthcoming.

00:37:02.738 --> 00:37:03.259
After that,

00:37:03.499 --> 00:37:04.019
by train

00:37:04.579 --> 00:37:05.600
via Magdeburg,

00:37:06.180 --> 00:37:07.701
We were taken to Leipzig.

00:37:12.105 --> 00:37:20.151
We were put back in the train car and we were rolling along like that.

00:37:23.273 --> 00:37:27.617
And that's what I forgot to mention previously,

00:37:28.117 --> 00:37:30.079
There was a girl who asked...

00:37:32.388 --> 00:37:33.670
To the supervisor,

00:37:35.292 --> 00:37:35.713
" Madam,

00:37:35.813 --> 00:37:37.956
How long are we going to travel like this?

00:37:38.737 --> 00:37:40.579
There are dead bodies among us,

00:37:40.599 --> 00:37:42.141
There are people who are dying,

00:37:42.142 --> 00:37:43.082
We can't take it anymore.

00:37:45.105 --> 00:37:46.527
And the answer was,

00:37:47.028 --> 00:37:47.348
" Well,

00:37:47.428 --> 00:37:49.371
until you all die.

00:37:51.900 --> 00:37:52.341
Well then,

00:37:52.342 --> 00:37:53.803
We no longer had any illusions.

00:37:54.463 --> 00:37:55.985
When we arrived at Mauthausen,

00:37:56.506 --> 00:38:02.213
We were made to undress from the beginning of the night to take our clothes away, supposedly for disinfection.

00:38:02.733 --> 00:38:03.836
So we were very cold.

00:38:04.175 --> 00:38:04.817
All night long,

00:38:04.876 --> 00:38:05.818
It was March 12th.

00:38:05.818 --> 00:38:06.619
It was very cold.

00:38:08.775 --> 00:38:09.015
And then,

00:38:09.075 --> 00:38:14.779
We see a long convoy of men passing by, coming from what was called the Russian camp.

00:38:15.099 --> 00:38:16.840
because it had been built by the Russians,

00:38:17.181 --> 00:38:18.482
which was in fact the turnaround,

00:38:18.622 --> 00:38:19.242
the infirmary.

00:38:20.043 --> 00:38:22.224
And they were ghosts.

00:38:22.384 --> 00:38:22.664
First of all,

00:38:22.684 --> 00:38:23.445
They were naked.

00:38:24.086 --> 00:38:26.709
So they had blankets on them, like the Muslims.

00:38:26.769 --> 00:38:27.129
like that,

00:38:27.570 --> 00:38:30.053
or some kind of towel tied around it,

00:38:30.894 --> 00:38:31.755
in front of the genitals.

00:38:32.316 --> 00:38:33.678
Then they simply didn't care.

00:38:33.718 --> 00:38:36.141
They didn't care about being naked.

00:38:37.342 --> 00:38:38.003
They were passing by,

00:38:38.103 --> 00:38:38.464
like that.

00:38:38.924 --> 00:38:40.046
It was epic.

00:38:47.483 --> 00:38:51.527
They gassed 3500 of them in those last eight days.

00:38:52.107 --> 00:38:54.269
not to mention all the others we killed here and there,

00:38:54.349 --> 00:38:57.792
But in this case, they were completely exterminated at the very end.

00:38:58.593 --> 00:39:00.735
So, of course, that didn't make us happy.

00:39:00.755 --> 00:39:05.038
And besides, it worried us about our own fate.

00:39:05.039 --> 00:39:05.559
We were saying to each other,

00:39:06.199 --> 00:39:09.022
There's no reason why we should be released when we're in the process of killing these people.

00:39:30.180 --> 00:39:34.082
And those who were alive,

00:39:35.083 --> 00:39:36.764
if you can call it living,

00:39:37.904 --> 00:39:39.485
We were the living dead,

00:39:41.586 --> 00:39:49.471
We were led on a walk and we arrived at a gate.

00:39:51.732 --> 00:39:53.913
the guards on each side,

00:39:54.573 --> 00:39:55.754
us in the middle.

00:39:57.911 --> 00:40:02.472
And the people who were inside the camp,

00:40:03.513 --> 00:40:04.533
in front of the gate,

00:40:05.653 --> 00:40:06.574
they told us,

00:40:07.374 --> 00:40:09.354
to announce some good news to us,

00:40:10.195 --> 00:40:13.456
The Germans are not allowed to enter this camp.

00:40:16.156 --> 00:40:18.157
And there is one among us,

00:40:19.357 --> 00:40:23.759
when she was just the foot.

00:40:27.840 --> 00:40:28.880
In that portal,

00:40:29.561 --> 00:40:35.363
She turned around and spat in the supervisor's face.

00:40:37.924 --> 00:40:40.605
I think we all would have wanted to do the same thing.

00:40:42.606 --> 00:40:50.450
But we were so exhausted that we no longer had the strength to move.

00:40:53.495 --> 00:40:57.239
And we were told that we were in Theresienstadt.

00:40:57.880 --> 00:40:59.101
in Czechoslovakia,

00:41:00.702 --> 00:41:04.026
and that we are protected in this camp by the Red Cross.

00:41:05.227 --> 00:41:07.769
And then suddenly we hear cries of joy,

00:41:08.230 --> 00:41:09.331
It was frantic,

00:41:09.992 --> 00:41:12.274
And those were the first ones, the ones in front of us.

00:41:13.595 --> 00:41:15.377
who arrived in...

00:41:16.799 --> 00:41:19.081
at the place where all the trucks were parked.

00:41:19.622 --> 00:41:20.904
And the truck drivers,

00:41:20.905 --> 00:41:24.748
They were American soldiers prisoners in their uniforms.

00:41:25.709 --> 00:41:26.971
And they were Black.

00:41:27.652 --> 00:41:29.214
So there are no black SS officers.

00:41:30.575 --> 00:41:32.457
It was insane.

00:41:32.757 --> 00:41:38.882
She wanted to embrace the poor Black people who couldn't love in the face of these filthy ghosts,

00:41:38.942 --> 00:41:39.422
filth,

00:41:39.502 --> 00:41:39.823
stinky

00:41:40.643 --> 00:41:42.244
who were retreating and saying to themselves,

00:41:42.565 --> 00:41:43.385
They're going to eat us alive.

00:41:44.186 --> 00:41:45.267
And so,

00:41:46.428 --> 00:41:46.948
It was crazy.

00:41:49.290 --> 00:41:49.630
Me too,

00:41:49.690 --> 00:41:50.451
when I arrived,

00:41:50.452 --> 00:41:53.053
I didn't want to kiss Black people.

00:41:53.093 --> 00:41:54.695
because there were people in front of me.

00:41:55.595 --> 00:41:55.775
SO,

00:41:55.776 --> 00:41:58.478
They gave us American cigarettes.

00:41:59.178 --> 00:42:00.099
The smell of cigarettes.

00:42:00.279 --> 00:42:00.659
I don't smoke.

00:42:00.719 --> 00:42:02.200
But that smell,

00:42:02.420 --> 00:42:03.101
when I feel it,

00:42:03.121 --> 00:42:04.341
I'm immersed again.

00:42:05.642 --> 00:42:08.263
I am free once again in Mattausen.

00:42:08.804 --> 00:42:12.046
And that's only on April 23rd.

00:42:12.846 --> 00:42:13.967
on the banks of the Elbe,

00:42:14.127 --> 00:42:20.891
But we had taken refuge in a house to be safe from the bombings,

00:42:23.172 --> 00:42:27.294
that I was liberated by the Red Army.

00:42:38.279 --> 00:42:39.280
And they were shouting at us,

00:42:39.780 --> 00:42:40.361
That's it,

00:42:40.401 --> 00:42:41.181
We are free.

00:42:42.863 --> 00:42:44.364
The Russian is arriving.

00:42:44.365 --> 00:42:51.590
Some of them were going crazy.

00:42:54.452 --> 00:42:56.494
I saw someone throw themselves over there,

00:42:58.035 --> 00:43:00.077
through this balcony,

00:43:01.578 --> 00:43:02.319
who fell.

00:43:08.808 --> 00:43:15.112
I think people didn't realize.

00:43:16.493 --> 00:43:19.555
I think they were crazy to do something like that.

00:43:20.116 --> 00:43:21.837
We said to each other in moments like these,

00:43:22.878 --> 00:43:24.659
Suicide is pointless.

00:43:29.604 --> 00:43:30.805
When we went outside,

00:43:31.845 --> 00:43:32.846
we checked,

00:43:33.186 --> 00:43:41.091
There was a baker's cart loaded with bread in front of the house.

00:43:41.251 --> 00:43:42.331
And on this bread,

00:43:43.232 --> 00:43:46.274
a soldier of the Red Army,

00:43:46.294 --> 00:43:47.615
legs apart,

00:43:47.855 --> 00:43:49.636
who launched the...

00:43:50.116 --> 00:43:55.325
the pine trees of the cart to the population that surrounded it.

00:43:55.365 --> 00:44:00.414
That's how we received our first Liberty Pine.

00:44:23.032 --> 00:44:36.303
And it was only from that moment on that repatriation options became available to us.

00:44:37.604 --> 00:44:41.087
And that's where I was already saying it,

00:44:41.187 --> 00:44:42.708
I did not choose Germany.

00:44:42.768 --> 00:44:44.690
I have chosen France again.

00:44:44.930 --> 00:44:45.651
I told everyone,

00:44:45.671 --> 00:44:46.691
I'm going to France.

00:44:49.053 --> 00:44:51.035
They looked at me as if I were crazy.

00:44:53.936 --> 00:44:55.237
A woman was telling me,

00:44:55.257 --> 00:44:56.157
But you're going to France,

00:44:56.217 --> 00:44:56.837
But do you...

00:44:57.657 --> 00:44:59.418
How are you going to get to France?

00:44:59.458 --> 00:45:00.638
Do you realize?

00:45:02.099 --> 00:45:03.839
We are in Czechoslovakia,

00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:05.960
France is far away.

00:45:08.461 --> 00:45:09.501
I didn't want to hear anything.

00:45:09.502 --> 00:45:10.561
I didn't want to know anything.

00:45:13.182 --> 00:45:16.123
From where the house came back to me,

00:45:17.583 --> 00:45:18.203
the parents,

00:45:18.243 --> 00:45:19.244
The discussions?

00:45:21.048 --> 00:45:24.469
who spoke of France as if it were the promised land,

00:45:25.569 --> 00:45:27.070
French culture,

00:45:27.150 --> 00:45:29.091
the French Revolution.

00:45:32.172 --> 00:45:37.173
My father, who had hoped to conduct an orchestra in Paris,

00:45:38.354 --> 00:45:39.754
He said it with a smile.

00:45:40.714 --> 00:45:42.075
without really believing it,

00:45:43.155 --> 00:45:43.695
But anyway.

00:46:01.354 --> 00:46:02.895
The rivalry wasn't fun.

00:46:03.515 --> 00:46:07.736
We felt like subhumans.

00:46:07.776 --> 00:46:08.296
animals,

00:46:08.696 --> 00:46:09.916
It was almost like being at camp.

00:46:10.737 --> 00:46:12.157
We were made to arrive in a line.

00:46:13.437 --> 00:46:14.538
We were sprinkled with...

00:46:16.178 --> 00:46:16.559
DTs,

00:46:16.560 --> 00:46:16.979
I believe,

00:46:17.400 --> 00:46:17.880
That was it.

00:46:18.481 --> 00:46:19.402
This white powder,

00:46:19.422 --> 00:46:19.542
there,

00:46:20.603 --> 00:46:20.744
Good,

00:46:20.745 --> 00:46:24.028
We eventually understood that they were afraid of typhus.

00:46:24.068 --> 00:46:25.890
but we still found it offensive.

00:46:26.250 --> 00:46:27.111
We were completely white.

00:46:28.093 --> 00:46:29.034
completely white hair

00:46:29.995 --> 00:46:30.956
It smelled bad.

00:46:31.056 --> 00:46:31.877
It was unpleasant.

00:46:31.897 --> 00:46:32.417
It stung.

00:46:32.418 --> 00:46:33.318
We were furious.

00:46:33.598 --> 00:46:34.799
And then at the end of the fifth day,

00:46:34.819 --> 00:46:35.199
I was told,

00:46:35.219 --> 00:46:35.339
Good,

00:46:35.359 --> 00:46:36.040
You go home.

00:46:36.881 --> 00:46:40.664
And so I boarded a train where there were only prisoners of war.

00:46:41.224 --> 00:46:42.285
So when they saw me,

00:46:42.286 --> 00:46:43.746
They asked me what I was doing there.

00:46:44.767 --> 00:46:46.368
and I told them I was a...

00:46:46.548 --> 00:46:47.850
They called me a German girl.

00:46:48.170 --> 00:46:49.711
What were you doing in Germany?

00:46:49.712 --> 00:46:50.131
they told me.

00:46:51.773 --> 00:46:52.213
For a little while,

00:46:52.214 --> 00:46:52.934
They would have beaten me.

00:46:53.014 --> 00:46:55.856
This is the first time since my arrest that I've been afraid.

00:46:56.316 --> 00:46:56.817
I thought to myself,

00:46:56.837 --> 00:46:57.697
I escaped from the camp.

00:46:57.737 --> 00:46:59.479
Those guys are going to rip me to shreds.

00:46:59.639 --> 00:47:00.860
And then in the transfer...

00:47:00.920 --> 00:47:02.001
to get from the train station to my house,

00:47:02.021 --> 00:47:03.421
We stopped at an aunt's house.

00:47:03.942 --> 00:47:12.987
At an aunt's house, who had summoned me when my mother told her I was resisting, to tell me that if ever,

00:47:13.327 --> 00:47:18.430
that I knew very well that the Germans had said that if they did not arrest the resistance fighters,

00:47:18.470 --> 00:47:19.810
They could arrest families.

00:47:19.870 --> 00:47:20.371
the brothers,

00:47:20.411 --> 00:47:20.831
the fathers,

00:47:21.271 --> 00:47:21.731
the cousins,

00:47:21.732 --> 00:47:22.352
the cousins,

00:47:22.552 --> 00:47:22.992
everyone.

00:47:23.412 --> 00:47:26.594
And that they wouldn't let themselves be arrested without having done anything wrong.

00:47:26.634 --> 00:47:28.055
that they would be forced to denounce me.

00:47:28.075 --> 00:47:28.695
She told me that,

00:47:28.735 --> 00:47:29.236
the aunt.

00:47:30.616 --> 00:47:31.797
And when we went back,

00:47:32.718 --> 00:47:38.202
We stopped by this aunt's house, who had always been a little unwell, to say hello.

00:47:38.882 --> 00:47:39.162
But me,

00:47:39.202 --> 00:47:44.486
I still remembered his warning.

00:47:44.966 --> 00:47:50.870
And what do I find when I get out of the car to give him a kiss on his radio?

00:47:51.270 --> 00:47:56.674
A beautiful photo of me all grown up like this with a lovely tricolour ribbon and a bow.

00:47:57.014 --> 00:47:58.515
I burst out laughing.

00:47:58.955 --> 00:47:59.836
I couldn't stop.

00:47:59.836 --> 00:48:02.979
I stopped laughing because I found it so ridiculous.

00:48:04.440 --> 00:48:10.186
Like this France, whether collaborating or passive,

00:48:10.206 --> 00:48:11.727
and then suddenly, heroically,

00:48:12.187 --> 00:48:16.091
with tricolour cockades on the photo of the heroes.

00:48:20.820 --> 00:48:21.741
My uncle told me,

00:48:22.122 --> 00:48:23.383
You know, they're all alive.

00:48:24.084 --> 00:48:24.785
And me, that's it.

00:48:25.065 --> 00:48:25.826
It killed me.

00:48:26.467 --> 00:48:27.148
All alive.

00:48:27.969 --> 00:48:30.612
So he wanted to talk about my parents, of course, and my family.

00:48:30.673 --> 00:48:32.855
But I was thinking about all the others there.

00:49:06.808 --> 00:49:12.271
I learned that my brother died a month before the liberation.

00:49:15.713 --> 00:49:16.953
that he let himself die.

00:49:20.535 --> 00:49:22.236
By saying that Frenia is no longer here,

00:49:24.557 --> 00:49:26.238
I no longer have a reason to live.

00:49:35.632 --> 00:49:36.513
When we returned,

00:49:37.373 --> 00:49:39.855
The Jewish problem was completely ignored.

00:49:40.355 --> 00:49:41.776
It was all about the resistance fighters.

00:49:42.717 --> 00:49:44.038
Jews did not exist.

00:49:45.038 --> 00:49:47.480
They came back just like any of us,

00:49:47.800 --> 00:49:48.681
no difference.

00:49:49.221 --> 00:49:50.462
And they were worse off...

00:49:50.502 --> 00:49:50.942
mistreated,

00:49:51.263 --> 00:49:52.484
because initially,

00:49:53.424 --> 00:49:55.486
They were not given a pension.

00:49:55.726 --> 00:49:58.589
Rather, they had the pension of what were called politicians.

00:49:58.629 --> 00:50:00.390
that is to say, a pittance,

00:50:00.751 --> 00:50:02.072
Therefore, they were misidentified.

00:50:02.152 --> 00:50:02.512
Often,

00:50:02.532 --> 00:50:03.553
They were foreigners.

00:50:03.953 --> 00:50:05.234
So they were having difficulties.

00:50:05.515 --> 00:50:06.315
Arrested in France,

00:50:06.335 --> 00:50:07.176
They were returning to France.

00:50:07.476 --> 00:50:09.638
People who had taken refuge from Poland or elsewhere,

00:50:10.759 --> 00:50:13.481
They were in incredibly difficult circumstances.

00:50:14.102 --> 00:50:15.783
And what's more, they were ashamed.

00:50:17.364 --> 00:50:18.184
That's for sure.

00:50:19.305 --> 00:50:23.026
Perhaps she was ashamed of not having fought.

00:50:23.606 --> 00:50:23.866
Yet,

00:50:23.886 --> 00:50:25.526
There were many Jews in the resistance.

00:50:25.586 --> 00:50:27.967
There was resistance to Moses,

00:50:27.987 --> 00:50:29.587
a significant Jewish resistance.

00:50:30.048 --> 00:50:31.188
But the vast majority of people,

00:50:31.248 --> 00:50:31.548
anyway,

00:50:32.088 --> 00:50:33.889
They were quite passive.

00:50:34.349 --> 00:50:34.829
In my opinion,

00:50:34.830 --> 00:50:35.929
They couldn't do otherwise.

00:50:36.049 --> 00:50:42.011
I can't picture a woman with four kids fighting off the police who came to arrest her.

00:50:42.012 --> 00:50:42.511
In addition,

00:50:42.571 --> 00:50:45.552
They were arrested by the French gendarmerie.

00:50:45.672 --> 00:50:46.432
almost all by himself.

00:50:46.752 --> 00:50:52.677
But this arbitrary separation also exists between resistance and genocide,

00:50:52.737 --> 00:50:57.221
whereas it was part of a broader policy,

00:50:59.302 --> 00:51:02.205
This is, in my opinion, a serious mistake.

00:51:03.586 --> 00:51:13.634
I think that perhaps history will restore some form of unity to the massacre.

00:51:13.734 --> 00:51:15.716
That's why I've always said...

00:51:16.276 --> 00:51:18.858
And I told them again that none of us,

00:51:18.918 --> 00:51:19.659
Normally,

00:51:20.559 --> 00:51:32.289
He should not return because a dictatorship prioritizes the elimination of opponents of the dictatorship.

00:51:32.349 --> 00:51:33.650
And sometimes,

00:51:33.690 --> 00:51:35.351
somewhat incidentally,

00:51:36.072 --> 00:51:37.453
scapegoats.

00:51:38.494 --> 00:51:38.694
Good,

00:51:38.794 --> 00:51:42.977
But that's already one thing.

00:51:43.058 --> 00:51:43.398
SO,

00:51:43.938 --> 00:51:45.880
I think things will still be okay...

00:51:46.741 --> 00:52:02.818
Indeed, it's better when we don't say, for example, to someone who was deported, "So you're Jewish," as if only Jews were deported.

00:52:02.898 --> 00:52:07.003
sometimes leads to this error as well

00:52:08.644 --> 00:52:09.124
So, me,

00:52:09.184 --> 00:52:09.845
for a long time,

00:52:10.305 --> 00:52:12.327
I didn't mention deportation.

00:52:12.507 --> 00:52:13.908
except when it was just the two of us.

00:52:14.748 --> 00:52:16.990
because I felt that people were interested,

00:52:17.270 --> 00:52:17.850
They didn't care.

00:52:17.851 --> 00:52:18.691
like in the year 40,

00:52:18.711 --> 00:52:20.492
There was no point in telling them the stuff.

00:52:21.172 --> 00:52:22.393
And then in 1980,

00:52:23.214 --> 00:52:23.374
THE...

00:52:23.614 --> 00:52:24.695
The negotiators,

00:52:24.956 --> 00:52:25.657
revisionists,

00:52:25.658 --> 00:52:26.317
we said first,

00:52:26.337 --> 00:52:34.768
And then later the deniers appeared in our institutions.

00:52:34.988 --> 00:52:35.709
We thought to ourselves,

00:52:35.710 --> 00:52:36.870
Something needs to be done.

00:52:37.090 --> 00:52:38.452
We know that things have been done.

00:52:38.492 --> 00:52:40.593
gas chambers, of which we know how many people were imprisoned.

00:52:41.974 --> 00:52:43.515
what concentration camps were like.

00:52:44.835 --> 00:52:46.796
We can at least make ourselves heard as much as they do.

00:52:47.757 --> 00:52:51.179
So we need to make sure people listen to us.

00:52:51.219 --> 00:52:51.999
Let us be heard.

00:52:52.820 --> 00:52:59.643
When we started testifying, we thought we would warn young people.

00:53:01.448 --> 00:53:03.089
We're going to tell them what happened.

00:53:03.309 --> 00:53:04.870
That will make them think.

00:53:05.790 --> 00:53:07.671
They will know how to vote.

00:53:08.431 --> 00:53:09.852
We were deluding ourselves.

00:53:11.572 --> 00:53:12.813
And gradually,

00:53:13.093 --> 00:53:16.214
When you see things deteriorating like that,

00:53:17.275 --> 00:53:22.717
and take this turn which is beyond our control.

00:53:24.878 --> 00:53:26.859
this religious twist,

00:53:26.919 --> 00:53:27.559
I would say.

00:53:30.657 --> 00:53:31.760
We are powerless.

00:53:32.421 --> 00:53:34.546
Our testimony is useless.

00:53:44.075 --> 00:53:55.458
But it's true that I no longer really know how to glimpse any hope today.

00:53:56.259 --> 00:54:04.821
When I think that we've embarked on preemptive wars,

00:54:06.462 --> 00:54:09.563
to wage humanitarian wars.

00:54:11.715 --> 00:54:11.875
Good,

00:54:12.656 --> 00:54:19.843
It's true that we no longer understand why people choose war for...

00:54:23.387 --> 00:54:23.887
I would say,

00:54:24.447 --> 00:54:28.769
to improve or import democracy,

00:54:28.849 --> 00:54:30.370
because, quite obviously,

00:54:30.430 --> 00:54:30.750
In my opinion,

00:54:31.651 --> 00:54:38.613
This is not the right solution to give humanity a future.

00:54:39.234 --> 00:54:41.515
Who benefits from wars?

00:54:41.835 --> 00:54:43.135
It's always the same thing.

00:54:45.616 --> 00:54:47.277
We believe we are dying for our country.

00:54:47.377 --> 00:54:48.277
Well, that's it.

00:54:48.398 --> 00:54:50.658
I think it doesn't exist anymore.

00:54:53.783 --> 00:54:57.265
People were already dying for heavy industry.

00:54:57.385 --> 00:55:00.247
whether it be the De Vendel family,

00:55:01.768 --> 00:55:02.729
the Krupp or

00:55:03.129 --> 00:55:06.191
Thyssen, and today it's the same,

00:55:06.371 --> 00:55:07.192
It's Enron.

00:55:09.273 --> 00:55:10.154
Papa Bush,

00:55:11.695 --> 00:55:18.680
Rumsfeld and the others who want Iraqi oil,

00:55:19.260 --> 00:55:21.101
who lied to wage war.

